From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:06:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally defer compute submissions
 only beside compute

With g16_submit_defer 2 and g16_submit_kick 16, a compute submission
that finds 2 to 15 compute flights out is left queued for a poll pass
on the worker instead of running its own pass. With only compute in
flight that pass publishes several submissions together and retires
what has finished. Measured on linux-aurora-next 1.1089 (experimental),
compute.light alone at depth 4 went from 50.28 to 42.55 us per
submission and at depth 16 from 24.60 to 22.38 us.

Beside a drawing client the same deferral only moves time between the
clients. On 1.1089, with compute.light and render.light both at depth 8,
compute went from 65.40 to 69.31 us per submission and render from
164.11 to 141.60 us, with the commands per second of both together
about unchanged (21.39k to 21.49k). Summed over that load, the GPU's
compute stage time fell 4.7 % and its TA and FS stage times rose
15.8 % and 16.1 %.

Add g16_submit_defer_render (runtime 0644, default 0). With N, while any
published flight holds a render, a compute submission is left queued
only from N compute flights up and never asks for a pass; the pair
applies as set only while every flight is compute. 16 gives a load with
renders the deferral of the old defaults. Render submissions are not
affected. A stats line counts the submissions decided with a render in
flight and those the word kept from being deferred. Nothing changes
while the word is 0.

The rule is in a core-only module with host tests.

Assisted-by: LLM
